Low-level (linear-memory wasm) classlib fixes found running Minecraft 26.2's server:
  Class.getEnumConstants returned a clone of the runtime's constants array, whose class is not E[], so the cast
  every caller makes ((E[]) X.class.getEnumConstants(), Minecraft's StaticAction) threw ClassCastException. The
  constants are now copied into a new E[].
  RandomAccessFile in a read-write mode threw FileNotFoundException for a missing file; the JDK creates it. And it
  truncated an existing file (the in-memory file system truncates every writable open that does not append), so
  Minecraft's region files read back empty and every saved chunk was regenerated without any error.
  Path.of(URI) / Paths.get(URI) went through FileSystems.getFileSystem(uri), which accepts only the root URI, so
  every other file: URI threw; the scheme's provider now resolves it (JDK semantics). (Not low-level specific.)
  Files.find concatenated a null stream for a non-matching directory (NPE) and emitted a matching one twice.
  The default file system's Path: iterator() returned null, equals(this) was false (so p.relativize(p) threw), and
  resolving against the empty path prepended a separator.
  Class.getSuperclass read JS-shaped metadata; on the low-level targets it now answers RuntimeClass.parent
  (Minecraft's SynchedEntityData numbers entity data by walking superclasses: "Duplicate id value for 0").
Codegen: these methods on the low-level targets only.

